    "lawCode": "Amd §209, Civ Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Civil Service Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S3524\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the civil service law, in relation to\nemployees classified as the Triborough bridge and tunnel authority\nsuperior officers benevolent association of an MTA-employer and the\nresolution of disputes in the course of collective negotiations\n\nPURPOSE:  To allow certified or registered public employee\norganizations to represent employees as the Triborough Bridge and\nTunnel Authority Superior Officer Benevolent Association of an\nMTA-public employer and to be covered by the provisions of section 209\nof the Civil Service Law.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends section 209 of the Civil Service Law to grant\nbinding arbitration to Triborough bridge and tunnel authority superior\nofficers benevolent association members.\n\nSection two states that this bill shall take effect immediately,\nprovided, however, that the amendments to paragraph (f) of section\n209(5) of the Civil Service Law made by section one of this bill shall\nnot affect the expiration of such subdivision and shall be deemed to\nexpire therewith.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:  Current provisions of Chapter 929 of the Laws of 1986\nrelating to compulsory arbitration to resolve impasses in collective\nnegotiations between an MTA public employer and a public employee\norganization left out certain employees from receiving this benefit.\nThis bill would correct this inequity.\n\nOver the years, Compulsory arbitration has allowed the people of New\nYork to enjoy uninterrupted services. All evaluations of the effects\nof this law have been positive and have advocated the continuation of\nthis process.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY: This is a new bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS: None.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nSection two states that this bill shall take effect immediately,\nprovided, however, that the amendments to paragraph (f) of section\n209(5) of the Civil Service Law made by section one of this bill shall\nnot affect the expiration of such subdivision and shall be deemed to\nexpire therewith.\n\n",
